WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:07.600
David, I know you think Trump won't be arrested,&nbsp;
but will he be investigated when he leaves office?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:12.560
So almost certainly there are going&nbsp;
to be investigations of Donald Trump's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:18.720
businesses. There's going to be a lot of financial&nbsp;
crime investigation. It's possible that even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:23.520
people close to Donald Trump are going&nbsp;
to go down. But, yeah, I still don't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:29.120
think you're ever going to see Trump in prison.
There are a lot of people who rightly are feeling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:38.240
that if Donald Trump isn't personally prosecuted,&nbsp;
that an injustice has been done. And I am not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:44.800
arguing that Trump has done nothing worthy of&nbsp;
being investigated and potentially charged with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:50.880
criminality. But this is not a country that does&nbsp;
that. And I know that that upsets lots of people.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:55.360
And some people like the fact that this is not a&nbsp;
country that every time you get a new president,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.360 --> 00:01:00.400
they investigate charge and potentially even in&nbsp;
prison the previous president. It's not a country&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:04.240
that does that. I don't think we're&nbsp;
going to see that. What we will see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:09.440
are investigations into Donald Trump's business&nbsp;
dealings and financial stuff. I think that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:15.440
Trump's enablers can and should be prosecuted&nbsp;
directly when it applies. This includes family.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:20.160
This includes Republican senators. This includes&nbsp;
other functionaries, people involved in enabling.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:26.320
Illegal activity, even if it's financially&nbsp;
illegal activity, if such activity exists,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:31.520
they should be harshly penalized. As far&nbsp;
as Trump goes, I don't think it'll touch&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:36.640
Trump. I think there's the real possibility&nbsp;
that his businesses will end up having to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:44.320
settle and pay absolutely massive fines. It's&nbsp;
conceivable that if you find people involved&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:49.040
in Trump's businesses caught red handed with&nbsp;
financial fraud, money laundering, whatever,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:54.400
it's possible they may end up convicted. I&nbsp;
just don't think it's going to touch Trump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.400 --> 00:02:00.000
and I don't think it's going to be for political&nbsp;
crimes. It'll be a tax evasion, money laundering,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:04.400
improper use of charities, which Donald&nbsp;
Trump has already been been caught doing.&nbsp;

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:10.160
I think it will be that type of thing. I do&nbsp;
believe that Trump is worried because Trump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.160 --> 00:02:14.240
doesn't know. We had a few reports from right&nbsp;
before the election that part of why Trump is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.240 --> 00:02:19.280
panicking is because he's worried that the rest&nbsp;
of his life will be riddled by investigations&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:22.560
and maybe he could end up in prison.
I just don't think he'll end up in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:28.000
prison. I think it's completely plausible that&nbsp;
you do see investigations of different kinds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:32.960
plague the rest of Donald Trump's life. Now,&nbsp;
on the other side, there's people asking about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:38.640
pardons. Couldn't Trump preemptively pardon&nbsp;
everybody who's likely to be wrapped up in this?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:42.560
You know, I think there's two things that&nbsp;
will prevent that from happening. No.&nbsp;

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:47.760
One, I don't think Trump really cares about these&nbsp;
people. Trump doesn't care about his supporters.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:53.600
It's not clear Trump even cares about&nbsp;
his enablers. And that's one part of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:58.240
it. The other part of this is Trump has not&nbsp;
shown himself to be detail oriented enough&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:03.760
to actually figure out who is it that I need to&nbsp;
grant blanket preemptive pardons for. So I don't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:08.240
think that Trump will do it. He may do it with&nbsp;
some. I don't think he will get to everybody. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:13.520
then the other reason I think you are going to see&nbsp;
a deluge of investigations and possible charges&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:19.600
after Trump is out of office when it comes to his&nbsp;
associates is look at how many Trump associates&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:26.800
were convicted while Donald Trump was in office&nbsp;
with the Department of Justice encumbered by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:32.240
Trump loyalists, running interference. Once&nbsp;
Trump is gone and you have a different Justice&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:36.720
Department, I think you will see many more Trump&nbsp;
acolytes go down. Now, the last thing I want to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:40.720
say about this, Joe Biden shouldn't be involved&nbsp;
in this at all. Remember when Trump was saying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:45.840
to Hillary during the twenty sixteen debates, if I&nbsp;
was president, you'd be locked up and we're going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:49.440
to investigate you and all of this stuff.
And in fact, while Trump was president,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:52.880
he tried to push the Justice Department.&nbsp;
Can't you investigate Biden? Can't you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:57.920
do this? Can't you do that? Joe Biden should&nbsp;
have no involvement whatsoever in any possible&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.920 --> 00:04:02.480
investigations of anybody associated with&nbsp;
Donald Trump. I don't believe Joe Biden will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:06.720
do that. Joe Biden has shown no interest in&nbsp;
that. He's shown no willingness to do that.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.520 --> 00:04:14.480
And to be perfectly frank, even if he liked the&nbsp;
idea of being involved in investigations of Trump,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:19.920
Joe Biden's going to have his hands more than full&nbsp;
trying to clean up the mess from from from Donald&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:25.440
Trump. And he will be plenty busy. And I believe&nbsp;
that the next Department of Justice will also be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:32.640
very, very busy. Look at what escaped the Trump&nbsp;
bubble while he was president that we learned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:37.760
about in terms of criminality. Imagine what we're&nbsp;
going to learn about once he's finally gone.

